<title>CANADA: Whirlpool patent invalid - Maytag.</title>
<headline>Whirlpool patent invalid - Maytag.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maytag Corp said on Tuesday it will fight a Canadian lawsuit filed by Whirlpool Corp and Whirlpool Canadian unit Inglis Ltd, saying that Whirlpool did not have a patent on certain washer models.</p>
<p>Whirlpool said earlier today that some washers built and marketed by Maytag and its affiliates violated Whirlpool's Canadian patent, which was issued in 1981.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe that the Whirlpool patent is invalid,&quot; Maytag spokesman Tom Schwartz said a telephone interview. &quot;It did not meet the requirements for the a patentable invention.&quot;  </p>
<p>The lawsuit involves a two-way agitator.</p>
<p>&quot;That agitator is not unique in the industry,&quot; Schwartz said.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
</text>
